course: dictionary
lesson: 1407
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Cardinal» is a good example. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: «The four cardinal points are north, east, south and west, and adding north-east, south-east, south-west and north-west makes eight.» The words cardinal points tell you this is about directions on a map, so cardinal means main or basic here.
explain: Check the job the word is doing. A cardinal can be a person or a bird, which are nouns. Cardinal can also describe a thing, as in «a cardinal rule», which makes it an adjective. Ask yourself: is it naming something, or describing it?
fact: A cardinal is a senior leader in the Roman Catholic Church who wears red and helps choose the Pope.
fact: A cardinal is also a bright red songbird of North America, and the male has a crest.
fact: As an adjective, «cardinal» means most important or basic, as in «a cardinal rule».
fact: In maths, a cardinal number is a counting number like one, two, three, not first, second or third.
fact: «Cardinal points» are north, south, east and west, and «cardinal» can also mean a deep red colour.
exercise: «The four cardinal points are north, east, south and west.» What are the cardinal points? | Senior leaders in the Church | Red birds that sing in gardens | Counting numbers | *The main directions on a map
exercise: In maths, what is a cardinal number? | A number written in red ink | A very large number | *A counting number like one, two, three | A number that shows order, like first, second, third
exercise: A church lesson says cardinals help choose the Pope. What is a cardinal in this sentence? | A north-facing window | *A senior church leader who wears red | A deep red colour | A bright red songbird
test: In a nature lesson in the USA, a cardinal is most likely to be what? | A counting number | A type of map | *A bright red songbird with a crest | A senior church leader
test: «The cardinal rule of the game is to play fair.» What does cardinal mean here? | A deep red colour | A senior church leader | A counting number | *Most important or basic
exam: In «a cardinal sin», what does cardinal mean? | Very cold | A red bird | *Most serious or basic | A counting number
